            "These cycles hardly change the total sunlight, only where and when it falls. But cool summers at high northern latitudes let the winter snow survive and build up ice sheets. The ice reflects sunlight, and the cold ocean absorbs more carbon dioxide, so a small orbital nudge is magnified into an ice age. Explore it in the orbit laboratory, and look at the real ice-core records.",
